## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end CAPA design focusing on data-feed integrity and cross-region policy latency.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with provenance for logs/traces
- Region-aware lifecycle and state transitions
- REST API linking CAPAs to evidence logs/traces
- Region-aware metrics: MTTR, recurrence, false positives, latency
- RCA template and canary rollout plan for policy updates

## Code Example
```javascript
interface CAPA {
  id: string;
  incidentId: string;
  region: string;
  tenantId: string;
  policyVersion: string;
  evidence: string[]; // logs/traces
  state: 'identified'|'investigating'|'contained'|'mitigated'|'closed';
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt: string;
  remediation?: string;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate data-feed integrity across regions during rollback?
- What trade-offs exist between rapid containment and thorough RCA in high-throughput systems?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a CAPA program for data privacy incidents in a multi-tenant, real-time pipeline, balancing compliance and engineering practicality.

## Key Concepts
- Data lineage and PII tagging across streaming pipelines
- Region-aware metrics and containment strategies
- Minimal REST API design for CAPA lifecycle
- RCA templates plus staged preventive actions (canaries)
- Versioned redaction policy rollbacks and automated checks

## Code Example
```javascript
type CAPARecord = {
  id: string;
  evidenceRefs: string[];
  dataLineage: string;
  redactionVersion: string;
  implicatedRegions: string[];
  tenantIds: string[];
  severity: string;
  status: 'detected'|'contained'|'verified'|'closed';
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt?: string;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate the effectiveness of the redaction rollback in production?
- Which metrics would you surface to product and compliance teams during a breach incident?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design end-to-end CAPA workflow for data privacy policy failures, including evidence capture and cross-tenant rollout.

## Key Concepts

- CAPA data modeling for evidence and artifacts
- Lifecycle state machine and ownership
- Minimal REST API design with linked logs/traces
- Tenant/region metrics for containment and recurrence
- RCA templates and canary rollout planning

## Code Example

```javascript
// CAPA core types (overview)
interface CAPA {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  evidence: string[];
  artifacts: string[];
  state: 'detected'|'triaged'|'in_progress'|'contained'|'closed';
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt?: string;
  links?: { type: string; url: string }[];
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you scale CAPA data stores across regions?
- How to ensure regulatory auditability and evidence integrity?
